## Hard rule — do not deviate from the CAALM dialog template

- **ALWAYS** use the Standard Dialog Structure below (cap, gradient header, `bg-slate-50` body, footer) for every new or updated dialog/modal.
- **NEVER** invent alternate dialog chrome: custom icon tiles, white flat headers, solid filled destructive CTAs that replace `.delete-btn`, mock-only layouts, or one-off shells that skip the cap / gradient header / slate body.
- Prefer shared helpers (`.glass-dialog-wizard-header`, `DeleteConfirmationDialog`, existing `DialogContent` patterns) over hand-rolled dialog shells.
- **ONLY** depart from this template when the user **explicitly** asks for a different dialog design in that request. A screenshot or product mock is not permission to abandon the template unless they say to follow the mock over CAALM chrome.
- When unsure, match `ActionDropdown.tsx` / `dialog-best-practices.mdc` first; ask before redesigning dialog chrome.

- All dialogs, modals, and popups in the application must follow the enterprise/professional UI design standards.
- When creating or updating any dialog, automatically apply the following structure:

## Standard Dialog Structure

### 1. Dialog Container

```tsx
<Dialog open={isOpen} onOpenChange={setIsOpen}>
  <DialogContent className="max-w-[600px] p-0 max-h-[90vh] flex flex-col overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 shadow-xl">
    {/* Professional Cap */}
    <div className="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-4 bg-[#d6d7d8] opacity-70 rounded-t-md" />

    {/* Header with gradient background */}
    <div className="sticky top-0 z-10 bg-linear-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 py-4 border-b border-slate-200 mt-4">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-3 px-6">
        {/* Title with icon */}
        <div className="flex items-center gap-3">
          <IconComponent className="w-5 h-5 text-[#0f5384]" />
          <DialogTitle className="text-xl font-semibold sidebar-gradient-text">
            Dialog Title
          </DialogTitle>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p className="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1 ml-14">
        Optional subtitle or description
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Scrollable Content */}
    <div className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-6 bg-slate-50">
      {/* Main content here */}
    </div>

    {/* Professional Footer */}
    <div className="px-6 py-4 bg-slate-50 border-t border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-end gap-3">
      <Button className="primary-btn px-3 sm:px-4">
        <Icon className="h-4 w-4" />
        Action
      </Button>
    </div>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

### Dismiss control

- Prefer the built-in corner **X** on `DialogContent` (`showCloseButton`, **on by default for all variants** including `destructive`).
- Do **not** add a footer Cancel button unless the user explicitly asks for one, or Cancel does more than dismiss (discard draft, abort upload, cancel an event with side effects).
- Destructive confirms: keep `variant="destructive"` (blocks overlay dismiss); rely on the corner X to close. Primary footer action is Delete / Confirm only.
- Destructive delete buttons use `.delete-btn` (soft red, same family as Expired badge) — not solid filled red.
- Pass `showCloseButton={false}` only when dismiss must be fully blocked.

## Required Design Elements

### Form inputs

Text inputs, selects, textareas, and search fields inside dialogs must use a visible `border-[0.25px] border-slate-300`. Do not leave them borderless on `bg-slate-50`. See `input-field-borders.mdc`.

### Professional Cap

- Always include a thin horizontal bar at the top: `<div className="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-4 bg-[#d6d7d8] opacity-70 rounded-t-md" />`
- This creates visual consistency and indicates an enterprise application

### Header Section

- Use gradient background: `bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50` (or `.glass-dialog-wizard-header`)
- Add `mt-4` to account for the professional cap bar
- Icon is placed directly next to the title in a flex container: `<div className="flex items-center gap-3">`
- Icon uses brand color: `text-[#0f5384]` (no circular background)
- Icon size: `w-5 h-5` for header icons
- Title uses `sidebar-gradient-text` for brand consistency
- Subtitle uses `text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1 ml-14` to align with title text (margin-left accounts for icon + gap)

### Content Section

- Scrollable area MUST use `bg-slate-50` background: `flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-6 bg-slate-50`
- The main content area in dialogs, popovers, and cards should always use `bg-slate-50` for visual consistency
- Use adequate padding (p-6 or p-4) for breathing room
- Group related content in nested cards with `bg-white rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-200` for contrast against the slate-50 background

### Footer Section

- Background: `bg-slate-50 border-t border-slate-200`
- Primary action on the right; omit Cancel when the corner X is present
- Use consistent button styling: `primary-btn px-3 sm:px-4` / `delete-btn` for destructive confirms

## Interactive Elements

### Hoverable Cards/Items

- Use subtle hover effects: `hover:bg-blue-50 hover:border-blue-300 transition-all duration-200`
- Add shadow on hover for depth: `shadow-sm hover:shadow-md`
- Use `group` class for coordinated hover states on parent and children

### Icons

- Use consistent icon sizing: `h-4 w-4` or `h-5 w-5` for most icons
- Header icons: Place directly next to title with `gap-3`, use `text-[#0f5384]` for brand color
- Colored icons: `text-[#0f5384]` (brand blue), `text-blue-600`, `text-green`, `text-slate-600` etc.
- For list items or cards, circular icon backgrounds can be used: `w-8 h-8 bg-blue-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center`

### Buttons

- Primary action buttons: `className="btn-primary px-3 sm:px-4"` (or `primary-btn` — same styles)
- **ALWAYS** include a Lucide icon (`h-4 w-4`) on `btn-primary` / `primary-btn` buttons — never text-only
- Use consistent spacing: `gap-3` between buttons

## Color Palette

- Primary: Blue gradient (from-blue-50 to-indigo-50)
- Background:
  - Main content areas: `bg-slate-50` (ALWAYS use in dialog/popover/card content sections)
  - Nested content cards: `bg-white` for contrast
  - Footer sections: `bg-slate-50`
- Borders: slate-200
- Text:
  - Primary: slate-900
  - Secondary: slate-600
  - Muted: slate-500
  - Headers: sidebar-gradient-text (brand colors)
- Accents: `#0f5384` (brand blue), blue-600, green, purple-600

## List/Event Items in Dialogs

When displaying lists or events in dialogs:

- Use cards with border-2 for emphasis
- Include gradient icon backgrounds
- Show metadata with icons (Clock, Users, etc.)
- Add chevron indicators for clickable items
- Use badges/tags for categories or status

Example structure:

```tsx
<button className="w-full text-left p-4 rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-200 bg-white hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50 transition-all duration-200 group shadow-sm hover:shadow-md">
  <div className="flex items-start gap-4">
    <div className="w-10 h-10 bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-100 to-indigo-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 group-hover:from-blue-200 group-hover:to-indigo-200 transition-colors">
      <Icon className="h-5 w-5 text-blue-600" />
    </div>
    <div className="flex-1 min-w-0">{/* Title and metadata */}</div>
    <ChevronRight className="h-5 w-5 text-slate-400 group-hover:text-blue-600 transition-colors" />
  </div>
</button>
```

## Consistency Requirements

- NEVER deviate from the CAALM dialog template unless the user explicitly requests a different design
- NEVER use plain DialogContent without the professional structure
- NEVER skip the cap bar at the top
- NEVER use flat backgrounds in headers - always use the gradient
- NEVER use circular icon backgrounds in dialog headers - icons should be placed directly next to the title
- NEVER use `bg-white` for main dialog/popover/card content areas - ALWAYS use `bg-slate-50`
- NEVER forget to make content areas scrollable for overflow
- ALWAYS include footer sections with proper background and borders
- ALWAYS use `bg-slate-50` for the scrollable content area in dialogs, popovers, and cards
- ALWAYS use `mt-4` on the header div to account for the professional cap bar
- ALWAYS place header icons directly next to title with `gap-3` and use `text-[#0f5384]` color
- ALWAYS use `ml-14` on subtitle paragraphs to align with the title text (accounts for icon + gap)
- ALWAYS use consistent spacing and padding throughout
- ALWAYS apply transition effects for interactive elements

## Glass Card Design

All cards and dialogs should use the glass-card style for a modern, professional appearance. See `global-style-guide.mdc` for glass-card patterns and page structure standards.

